    "lawCode": "Add §92-d, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6398\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to granting\nsick leave for officers and employees with a qualifying World Trade\nCenter condition\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill provides officers and employees who participated in the\nrescue, recovery or cleanup of the World Trade Center and subsequently\ndeveloped a qualifying condition sick leave without loss of accrued\nsick leave.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of this bill amends the General Municipal Law to add a new\nsection 92-d to provide officers and employees who participated in the\nrescue, recovery or cleanup of the World Trade Center and subsequently\ndeveloped a qualifying condition shall receive line of duty sick\nleave.\n\nSection two of this bill provides that this act shall take effect on\nthe ninetieth day after it shall have become a law; provided, however,\nthat effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or repeal of\nany rule or regulation necessary for the implementation of this act on\nits effective date is authorized and directed to be made and completed\non or before such effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nOfficers and employees of municipal corporations or public authority\nrisked their wellbeing when they helped rescue and recover bodies\nwhile cleaning up the World Trade Center after tragedy hit New York\nCity. Over the last sixteen years, these brave individuals are facing\na multitude of health issues and require several doctor visits and\ntime off. Although we cannot cure them of their illnesses, we must\nrecognize their ultimate sacrifice and try our best to alleviate their\nissues. This legislation would ensure they have a line of duty sick\nleave and they are compensated at their normal rate of pay.\nFurthermore, such sick leave shall be provided without losing their\naccrued sick leave.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law; provided, however, that effective immediately, the\naddition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary\nfor the implementation of this act on its effective date is authorized\nand directed to be made and completed on or before such effective\ndate.\n",
