    "lawCode": "Add §92-d, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6398A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to granting\nsick leave for officers and employees with a qualifying World Trade\nCenter condition\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill provides officers and employees who participated in the\nrescue, recovery or cleanup of the World Trade Center and subsequently\ndeveloped a qualifying condition with line of duty sick leave so that\nthey do not lose of accrued sick leave for such condition.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of this bill amends the General Municipal Law to add a new\nsection 92-d to provide officers and employees of the State, a public\nauthority or a municipality of less than one million people who\nparticipated in the World Trade Center rescue, recovery or cleanup\nactivities and subsequently developed a qualifying condition with\nreceive line of duty sick leave. An employee who switched employers\nafter participating in the World Trade Center rescue, recovery or\ncleanup activities will still be eligible for the line of duty sick\nleave.\n\nSection two of this bill provides that the public authorities and\nmunicipalities shall be reimbursed by the State for any line of duty\nsick leave used.\n\nSection three of this bill provides that. his act shall take effect\nimmediately; provided, however, that any officer or employee who is\ncurrently employed by the State, public authority, municipal\ncorporation who has been diagnosed with a qualifying World Trade\nCenter condition and is using sick leave due to such condition shall\nreceive a restoration of such sick leave retroactive to the date such\nofficer or employee was diagnosed with a qualifying World Trade Center\ncondition.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nOfficers and employees of the State, public authorities and\nmunicipalities outside New York City risked their well-being when they\nhelped rescue and recover bodies while cleaning up the World Trade\nCenter after tragedy hit New York City.  Over the last sixteen years,\nthese brave individuals have faced, and are currently facing, a\nmultitude of health issues that require several doctor visits and time\noff. Although we cannot cure them of their illnesses, we must\nrecognize their ultimate sacrifice and try our best to help them\nduring these difficult times. This legislation would ensure they have\na line of duty sick leave so that they can receive treatment for the\nillness and convalesce without loss of their accrued sick leave.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that any\nofficer or employee who is currently employed by the State, public\nauthority, municipal corporation who has been diagnosed with a\nqualifying World Trade Center condition and is using sick leave due to\nsuch condition shall receive a restoration of such sick leave\nretroactive to the date such officer or employee was diagnosed with a\nqualifying World Trade Center condition.\n",
